cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Combusta in research, theses, or engineering reports, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Combusta: Fuel-Agnostic Engine Combustion Analysis, Case Comparison, and Verification & Validation Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  Combusta is a Python library for the analysis of internal combustion engine
  cycles from CFD and test-bench data. It provides a source-independent engine
  case model, single-zone heat-release analysis with temperature- and
  composition-dependent gas properties for any CxHyOz fuel including hydrogen,
  cycle metrics (IMEP, indicated efficiency, specific fuel consumption, burn
  fractions), side-by-side comparison of engine configurations with a
  significance test against numerical uncertainty, exhaust-emission
  post-processing, Grid Convergence Index estimation (Celik et al., 2008), and
  validation comparisons following ASME V&V 20-2009. Application modules cover
  diesel auto-ignition, spray tip penetration, standard-atmosphere altitude
  scaling, and Second-Law exergy analysis.
authors:
